  "summary": "ACCEPT. S12-4-PR-001 is closed by distinct pair-specific Flow Group and business-flow-logical-key/1.0 identities, a source-semantic ConsumerEntryStableKey, existing Logical Document uniqueness/current-pointer concurrency, explicit schema evolution, and cross-pair Version Chain tests. S12-4-PR-002 is closed by aggregating all provider evidence occurrences under one current provider XML Document Version before cardinality, preserving reconstructable contribution rows, and retaining ambiguity for distinct provider Documents. S12-4-PR-003 is closed by the new versioned CrossRepositoryResolutionDecision: endpoint/consumer-entry decisions own exact evidence, many exact-match decisions may reference one existing tuple-unique document-level REFERENCES Edge, Flow Groups bind one unique decision plus a reusable Edge, legacy one-to-one ExactCrossRepositoryEdgeEvidence remains unchanged, and migration/replay/tests cover same-pair multiplicity and pre-existing Edge reuse. The complete plan set is feasible and internally consistent with the specification, Story 12.1-12.3 seams, repository graph constraints, immutable Version Chains, atomic PostgreSQL behavior, bounded retrieval and strict Worker transport, security/data stewardship, migration compatibility, qualification strategy, failure isolation, replay, and Story 12.5 exclusions. No Critical/High finding, Constitution MUST violation, authority conflict, unresolved design question, or placeholder remains. All three planned-change triggers are accurate and require one explicit user authorization now, before task generation: the exact-resolution/grouping/scheduling Scan strategy, the new retrieve_code_logic and submit_business_logic Worker Agent tools, and the dated FR-4.5/FR-6.1/FR-6.2 replacement. That authorization advances only to tasks and does not waive definition review, implementation approval, TDD, convergence, quality, E2E, security, migration, provider qualification, or final verification. The nonrecursive boundary identity is SHA-256 over sorted path-tab-file-SHA256 lines for the nine pinned raw definition artifacts."
